  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 138 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nAs Wednesday approaches, we expect to see an increase in lower and\nmid level moisture along with a slight weakening of afternoon wind\nspeeds. This along with a upward bump in temperatures may push\nareas generally along and east of I-35 into Heat Advisory\ncriteria. While heat index values of 108 degrees are expected to\nbe the greater concern, we could also see a few locations reach\n103 degrees on Wednesday. \n\nThe forecast for Thursday into Saturday will depend on what\ntranspires in the Gulf. It is too early to tell what impacts may\noccur across south central Texas, so stay tuned to the forecast\nthis week. For now, we will not show much in the way of rain\nchances, but this may certainly change with subsequent forecasts.\nTemperatures look to remain near or above normal and we may need \nto monitor Thursday for additional heat headlines. \n\nFor the remainder of the forecast period, mid and upper level high\npressure remain the dominant weather feature over south central\nTexas. This should result in dry weather along with seasonal\ntemperatures.",
